  "domain": "Document review",
  "domainId": "document-review",
  "reviewDomain": "document-review",
  "question": "Does a document of this type contain what it must, and who checks each part of it?",
  "summary": "A reference template: what a product change document must contain, the rules those chapters have to satisfy, and all ten analyzers wired onto them with CHECKS. Two rules are joined by CONTRADICTS - consumer-only eligibility in one chapter, business tariffs eligible in another - which is the finding the Cross-Examiner exists to raise. Entirely invented: no organisation, product, customer or system appears anywhere in it.",
  "anonymised": true,
